strengths.value:
1. for the first time, the effect of neural populations, i.e., activation vectors, generated by different prompt stimuli, on inference is studied in representation space and its relevance is demonstrated
2. ablation experiments demonstrate that for problems with higher perplexity, the introduction of RoT produces a more significant improvement;
3. a new error localization method is proposed and validated

